## Future Work Behavior

& [JustificationBehavior] is the required behavior while implementing future work
  + [before_work] is the act of identifying the specification requirement being served
  + [during_work] is the act of preserving evidence and avoiding scope drift
  + [after_work] is the act of updating or adding [JustificationEntry]
  + [claim_check] is the final distinction between implemented, verified, partial, or specified-only

  = must: identify [requirement_anchor] before starting a substantial implementation step
  = must: update [implemented_artifact] after the work exists on disk
  = must: record [verification_result] after inspection, command output, test, or review
  = must: mark runtime work as [partially_justified] until a truth test or focused verification passes
  = must: mark documentation-only work as [justified] when it directly satisfies a documentation or specification requirement
  = must: mark runtime behavior as [specified_only] when it exists only as a document
  = should: append one new [JustificationEntry] per coherent feature or requirement group
  = should: keep entries small enough that progress can be audited without rereading the whole project

## Claim Discipline

& [CompletionClaimDiscipline] is the guardrail against false completion
  + [implemented] is work that exists in the repository
  + [verified] is implemented work that has passed a relevant check
  + [specified] is work described by a requirement but not yet implemented
  + [justified] is work whose implementation and verification satisfy the cited requirement

  = must: say implemented only when the artifact exists
  = must: say verified only when a check has been run or an inspection result exists
  = must: say specified only when the work remains a plan
  = must: say justified only when the evidence matches the requirement
  - never: let a clean narrative replace evidence
